    <ul class="statute-block__list">
      <li><a href="https://www.leg.state.fl.us/statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&amp;URL=0600-0699%2F0689%2FSections%2F0689.01.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Florida Statutes §689.01</strong></a> &mdash; deed execution and witness requirements</li>
      <li><a href="https://leg.state.fl.us/Statutes/index.cfm/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&amp;URL=0600-0699%2F0695%2FSections%2F0695.03.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Florida Statutes §695.03</strong></a> &mdash; acknowledgment and proof of deeds for recording</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.leg.state.fl.us/Statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&amp;URL=0600-0699%2F0695%2FSections%2F0695.01.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Florida Statutes §695.01</strong></a> &mdash; recording's effect against creditors and subsequent purchasers</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.leg.state.fl.us/statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&amp;URL=0200-0299%2F0201%2FSections%2F0201.02.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Florida Statutes §201.02</strong></a> &mdash; documentary stamp tax on deeds</li>
